{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lm3VKmA24wFl4he0FKQic5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<canvas id=\"0:1\" name=\"00 · Start Here 设计任务\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\">\n  <frame id=\"8:2\" name=\"Start Here · Brief\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1440\" height=\"5164\">\n    <frame id=\"8:3\" name=\"Header\" x=\"64\" y=\"64\" width=\"1312\" height=\"145\">\n      <text id=\"8:4\" name=\"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"182\" height=\"19\" />\n      <text id=\"8:5\" name=\"Foodieland — recipe and food blog website\" x=\"0\" y=\"31\" width=\"1312\" height=\"52\" />\n      <text id=\"8:6\" name=\"Design a recipe website: discover featured and popular recipes, open a recipe with its ingredients and directions, browse and read blog articles, and contact the team. Desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\" x=\"0\" y=\"95\" width=\"1312\" height=\"50\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"8:7\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"64\" y=\"257\" width=\"1312\" height=\"249\">\n      <text id=\"8:8\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"147\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"8:9\" name=\"1. Build exactly the 5 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The two brand colors and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button and a default Text Field. Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the wordmark, the social logos, the photos, the category images, the decorations, the avatars and the icons from 04 · Media. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"198\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"8:10\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\"64\" y=\"554\" width=\"1312\" height=\"1925\">\n      <text id=\"8:11\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"413\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"8:12\" name=\"Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <frame id=\"8:13\" name=\"Frame cards\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"1836\">\n        <frame id=\"8:14\" name=\"01_Home\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"756\">\n          <text id=\"8:15\" name=\"01_Home\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"82\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"8:16\" name=\"Goal: Find something to cook today.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:17\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:18\" name=\"• Categories: “Categories” · “View All Categories” · Breakfast · Vegan · Meat · Dessert · Lunch · Chocolate, each with its image (Category_Breakfast … Category_Chocolate) • Chef promo: “Everyone can be a chef in their own kitchen” · copy (see DATA) · “Learn More” · Photo_Chef · Decor_Tomato · Decor_Onion • Featured recipe: “Hot Recipes” (Icon_Hot_Recipes) · “Spicy delicious chicken wings” · copy (see DATA) · 30 Minutes (Icon_Timer) · Chicken (Icon_Fork_Knife) · Avatar_John_Smith · John Smith · 15 March 2022 · “View Recipes” (Icon_Play) · Photo_Hero_Chicken_Wings · round badge “Handpicked Recipes” • Footer: see DATA (Footer) • Header: Logo_Foodieland · navigation Home / Recipes / Blog / Contact / About us · current: Home · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram • Instagram: “Check out @foodieland on Instagram” · copy (see DATA) · 4 posts, each with Avatar_Foodieland · “Foodieland.” · “Tokyo, Japan” · more (Icon_More) · photo · photo counter 1/3 · like (Icon_Like) · comment (Icon_Comment) · share (Icon_Send) · save (Icon_Save) · “Liked by craig_love and 44,686 others” · caption · “September 19” (see DATA) · “Visit Our Instagram” (Logo_Instagram) • More recipes: “Try this delicious recipe to make your day” · copy (see DATA) · 8 recipe cards with photo, title, time (Icon_Timer), category (Icon_Fork_Knife) and favorite (Icon_Favorite) · favorited: as marked in DATA • Newsletter: “Deliciousness to your inbox” · copy (see DATA) · email field “Your email address...” · “Subscribe” · Decor_Subscribe_Vegetables · Decor_Subscribe_Leaf · Decor_Subscribe_Salad • Simple and tasty recipes: “Simple and tasty recipes” · copy (see DATA) · 8 recipe cards with photo, title, time (Icon_Timer), category (Icon_Fork_Knife) and favorite (Icon_Favorite) · favorited: as marked in DATA · promo card: “Don’t forget to eat healthy food” · “www.foodieland.com” · Photo_Ad_Salad\" x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"596\" height=\"520\" />\n          <text id=\"8:19\" name=\"LINKS\" x=\"24\" y=\"646\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:20\" name=\"→ “Healthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus” card → 02_Recipe → Blog (nav) → 03_Blog → Contact (nav) → 05_Contact\" x=\"24\" y=\"672\" width=\"596\" height=\"60\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:21\" name=\"02_Recipe\" x=\"668\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"716\">\n          <text id=\"8:22\" name=\"02_Recipe\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"93\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"8:23\" name=\"Goal: Follow the recipe for Healthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:24\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:25\" name=\"• Actions: “PRINT” (Icon_Print) · “SHARE” (Icon_Share) • Directions: “Directions” · 3 steps, each with checkbox, number, title and text; step 1 also has Photo_Cooking_Step (see DATA) • Footer: see DATA (Footer) • Header: Logo_Foodieland · navigation Home / Recipes / Blog / Contact / About us · current: Recipes · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram • Ingredients: “Ingredients” · “For main dish” 5 items · “For the sauce” 3 items · each with a checkbox · checked: the first main-dish item (Icon_Check) (see DATA) • Intro: one paragraph (see DATA) • Media: Photo_Japanese_Fried_Rice as the recipe video cover · play (Icon_Play) • Meta: Avatar_John_Smith · John Smith · 15 March 2022 · “PREP TIME” 15 Minutes (Icon_Timer) · “COOK TIME” 15 Minutes (Icon_Timer) · Healthy (Icon_Fork_Knife) • Newsletter: “Deliciousness to your inbox” · copy (see DATA) · email field “Your email address...” · “Subscribe” · Decor_Subscribe_Vegetables · Decor_Subscribe_Leaf · Decor_Subscribe_Salad • Nutrition Information: Calories 219.9 kcal · Total Fat 10.7 g · Protein 7.9 g · Carbohydrate 22.3 g · Cholesterol 37.4 mg · note (see DATA) • Other Recipe: “Other Recipe” · Chicken Meatballs with Cream Cheese · The Creamiest Creamy Chicken and Bacon Pasta · The Best Easy One Pot Chicken and Rice, each with photo and “By Andreas Paula” • Promo card: “Don’t forget to eat healthy food” · “www.foodieland.com” · Photo_Ad_Salad • Recommended recipes: “You may like these recipes too” · the first 4 cards of “More recipes” in DATA, each with photo, title, time (Icon_Timer), category (Icon_Fork_Knife) and favorite (Icon_Favorite) • Title: “Healthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus”\" x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"596\" height=\"500\" />\n          <text id=\"8:26\" name=\"LINKS\" x=\"24\" y=\"626\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:27\" name=\"→ Home (nav) → 01_Home → Blog (nav) → 03_Blog\" x=\"24\" y=\"652\" width=\"596\" height=\"40\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:28\" name=\"03_Blog\" x=\"0\" y=\"780\" width=\"644\" height=\"556\">\n          <text id=\"8:29\" name=\"03_Blog\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"73\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"8:30\" name=\"Goal: Find an article to read.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:31\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:32\" name=\"• Articles: 6 articles, each with photo, title, excerpt, author avatar, author name and date (see DATA) • Footer: see DATA (Footer) • Header: Logo_Foodieland · navigation Home / Recipes / Blog / Contact / About us · current: Blog · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram • Newsletter: “Deliciousness to your inbox” · copy (see DATA) · email field “Your email address...” · “Subscribe” · Decor_Subscribe_Vegetables · Decor_Subscribe_Leaf · Decor_Subscribe_Salad • Page intro: “Blog &amp; Article” · “Recipes, kitchen tips and stories from the Foodieland team.” • Pagination: 1 · 2 · 3 · 4 · 5 · … · next (Icon_Chevron_Right) · current: 1 • Promo card: “Don’t forget to eat healthy food” · “www.foodieland.com” · Photo_Ad_Salad • Search: field “Search article, news or recipe...” · “Search” • Tasty Recipes: “Tasty Recipes” · Chicken Meatballs with Cream Cheese (Photo_Chicken_Meatballs) · Traditional Bolognaise Ragu (Photo_Creamy_Chicken_Bacon_Pasta) · Pork and Chive Chinese Dumplings (Photo_Dumplings), each with “By Andreas Paula”\" x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"596\" height=\"340\" />\n          <text id=\"8:33\" name=\"LINKS\" x=\"24\" y=\"466\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:34\" name=\"→ “Full Guide to Becoming a Professional Chef” → 04_Blog_Post → Home (nav) → 01_Home\" x=\"24\" y=\"492\" width=\"596\" height=\"40\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:35\" name=\"04_Blog_Post\" x=\"668\" y=\"780\" width=\"644\" height=\"496\">\n          <text id=\"8:36\" name=\"04_Blog_Post\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"122\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"8:37\" name=\"Goal: Read the article “Full Guide to Becoming a Professional Chef”.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:38\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:39\" name=\"• Article header: “Full Guide to Becoming a Professional Chef” · Avatar_Dianne_Russell · Dianne Russell · 12 November 2021 · intro (see DATA) · Photo_Blog_Chef • Article: 5 questions with answers, a pull quote and Photo_Cooking_Step after the third answer (see DATA) • Footer: see DATA (Footer) • Header: Logo_Foodieland · navigation Home / Recipes / Blog / Contact / About us · current: Blog · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram • Newsletter: “Deliciousness to your inbox” · copy (see DATA) · email field “Your email address...” · “Subscribe” · Decor_Subscribe_Vegetables · Decor_Subscribe_Leaf · Decor_Subscribe_Salad • Recommended recipes: “Check out the delicious recipes” · the first 4 cards of “More recipes” in DATA, each with photo, title, time (Icon_Timer), category (Icon_Fork_Knife) and favorite (Icon_Favorite) • Share: “SHARE THIS ON:” · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram\" x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"596\" height=\"280\" />\n          <text id=\"8:40\" name=\"LINKS\" x=\"24\" y=\"406\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:41\" name=\"→ Blog (nav) → 03_Blog → recommended recipe “Healthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus” → 02_Recipe\" x=\"24\" y=\"432\" width=\"596\" height=\"40\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:42\" name=\"05_Contact\" x=\"0\" y=\"1360\" width=\"644\" height=\"476\">\n          <text id=\"8:43\" name=\"05_Contact\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"103\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"8:44\" name=\"Goal: Send the team a message.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:45\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:46\" name=\"• Contact form: “Contact us” · NAME (placeholder “Enter your name...”) · EMAIL ADDRESS (“Your email address...”) · SUBJECT (“Enter subject...”) · ENQUIRY TYPE: Advertising (Icon_Chevron_Down) · MESSAGE (“Enter your message...”) · “Submit” · Photo_Chef_Contact • Footer: see DATA (Footer) • Header: Logo_Foodieland · navigation Home / Recipes / Blog / Contact / About us · current: Contact · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram • Newsletter: “Deliciousness to your inbox” · copy (see DATA) · email field “Your email address...” · “Subscribe” · Decor_Subscribe_Vegetables · Decor_Subscribe_Leaf · Decor_Subscribe_Salad • Recommended recipes: “Check out the delicious recipes” · the first 4 cards of “More recipes” in DATA, each with photo, title, time (Icon_Timer), category (Icon_Fork_Knife) and favorite (Icon_Favorite)\" x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"596\" height=\"260\" />\n          <text id=\"8:47\" name=\"LINKS\" x=\"24\" y=\"386\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:48\" name=\"→ Home (nav) → 01_Home → recommended recipe “Healthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus” → 02_Recipe\" x=\"24\" y=\"412\" width=\"596\" height=\"40\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"8:49\" name=\"Navigation structure\" x=\"64\" y=\"2527\" width=\"1312\" height=\"205\">\n      <text id=\"8:50\" name=\"Navigation structure\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"242\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"8:51\" name=\"• Header on all 5 frames: Logo_Foodieland, then Home / Recipes / Blog / Contact / About us, then Facebook, Twitter and Instagram. Current: Home on 01, Recipes on 02, Blog on 03 and 04, Contact on 05. How the current item looks is yours. • Footer on all 5 frames. Newsletter card on all 5 frames. • Flow: 01_Home → recipe card → 02_Recipe. Blog → 03_Blog → article → 04_Blog_Post. Contact → 05_Contact. Recommended-recipe cards on 02, 04 and 05 lead to 02_Recipe for the fried rice; other cards are entry only. • Entry only (no frame): Recipes (the list) and About us in the nav, social logos, View Recipes, View All Categories, category tiles, other recipe cards, favorites, Learn More, Instagram post actions, Visit Our Instagram, PRINT, SHARE, play, checkboxes, Other Recipe / Tasty Recipes items, promo card, search, pagination, other articles, form fields, Submit, Subscribe.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"154\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"8:52\" name=\"Fixed data &amp; copy\" x=\"64\" y=\"2780\" width=\"1312\" height=\"1611\">\n      <text id=\"8:53\" name=\"Fixed data &amp; copy\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"207\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"8:54\" name=\"Use these values verbatim.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <frame id=\"8:55\" name=\"Data blocks\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"1522\">\n        <frame id=\"8:56\" name=\"Home copy\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"296\">\n          <text id=\"8:57\" name=\"Home copy\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:58\" name=\"Featured: Crispy outside, juicy inside and coated in a sticky, spicy glaze — these wings are ready in 30 minutes and disappear even faster. Simple and tasty recipes: Quick, everyday dishes with ingredients you can find at any supermarket. Chef promo: Step-by-step recipes, clear timings and tips from our cooks help you make restaurant-quality food at home. Instagram: Follow us for daily recipe ideas, behind-the-scenes cooking and photos from our community. More recipes: Fresh ideas for breakfast, lunch and dinner — pick one and get cooking.\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"228\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:59\" name=\"Simple and tasty recipes (01, in order; ♥ = favorited)\" x=\"444\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"372\">\n          <text id=\"8:60\" name=\"Simple and tasty recipes (01, in order; ♥ = favorited)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"359\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:61\" name=\"Big and Juicy Wagyu Beef Cheeseburger · 30 Minutes · Western · ♥ (Photo_Wagyu_Cheeseburger) Fresh Lime Roasted Salmon with Ginger Sauce · 30 Minutes · Fish (Photo_Lime_Salmon) Strawberry Oatmeal Pancake with Honey Syrup · 30 Minutes · Breakfast (Photo_Strawberry_Oatmeal_Pancake) Fresh and Healthy Mixed Mayonnaise Salad · 30 Minutes · Healthy · ♥ (Photo_Mayonnaise_Salad) Chicken Meatballs with Cream Cheese · 30 Minutes · Meat (Photo_Chicken_Meatballs) Fruity Pancake with Orange &amp; Blueberry · 30 Minutes · Sweet · ♥ (Photo_Fruity_Pancake) The Best Easy One Pot Chicken and Rice · 30 Minutes · Snack (Photo_One_Pot_Chicken_Rice) The Creamiest Creamy Chicken and Bacon Pasta · 30 Minutes · Noodles (Photo_Creamy_Chicken_Bacon_Pasta)\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"304\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:62\" name=\"More recipes (01, in order; ♥ = favorited)\" x=\"888\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"372\">\n          <text id=\"8:63\" name=\"More recipes (01, in order; ♥ = favorited)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"280\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:64\" name=\"Mixed Tropical Fruit Salad with Superfood Boosts · 30 Minutes · Healthy · ♥ (Photo_Tropical_Fruit_Salad) Big and Juicy Wagyu Beef Cheeseburger · 30 Minutes · Western (Photo_Wagyu_Cheeseburger_Alt) Healthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus · 30 Minutes · Healthy (Photo_Japanese_Fried_Rice) Cauliflower Walnut Vegetarian Taco Meat · 30 Minutes · Eastern (Photo_Cauliflower_Taco) Rainbow Chicken Salad with Almond Honey Mustard Dressing · 30 Minutes · Healthy · ♥ (Photo_Rainbow_Chicken_Salad) Barbeque Spicy Sandwiches with Chips · 30 Minutes · Snack (Photo_Barbeque_Sandwiches) Firecracker Vegan Lettuce Wraps - Spicy! · 30 Minutes · Vegan (Photo_Vegan_Lettuce_Wraps) Chicken Ramen Soup with Mushroom · 30 Minutes · Japanese · ♥ (Photo_Chicken_Ramen)\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"304\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:65\" name=\"Instagram posts (01, in order)\" x=\"0\" y=\"396\" width=\"420\" height=\"258\">\n          <text id=\"8:66\" name=\"Instagram posts (01, in order)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"202\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:67\" name=\"1. Photo_Instagram_1 — The vegetable dishes need to have certain vitamins for those people 2. Photo_Instagram_2 — Sweet food can bring someone happiness, as long as they don’t eat too much 3. Photo_Instagram_3 — What do you do before you start cooking? Prepare the tools or the ingredients? 4. Photo_Instagram_4 — Steak is never wrong; it’s perfect if you want a romantic dinner All: Foodieland. · Tokyo, Japan · 1/3 · Liked by craig_love and 44,686 others · September 19\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"190\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:68\" name=\"Recipe (02) · intro &amp; nutrition\" x=\"444\" y=\"396\" width=\"420\" height=\"163\">\n          <text id=\"8:69\" name=\"Recipe (02) · intro &amp; nutrition\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"198\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:70\" name=\"Intro: A quick weeknight fried rice that turns leftover rice into a light, healthy meal. Crisp asparagus, soft eggs and a simple soy-sesame sauce come together in one pan in about 30 minutes. Nutrition note: Values are per serving and approximate.\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"95\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:71\" name=\"Recipe (02) · ingredients\" x=\"888\" y=\"396\" width=\"420\" height=\"144\">\n          <text id=\"8:72\" name=\"Recipe (02) · ingredients\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"169\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:73\" name=\"For main dish: 2 cups cooked jasmine rice, chilled overnight (checked) · 1 bunch asparagus, cut into 2 cm pieces · 2 eggs, beaten · 2 spring onions, thinly sliced · 1 tbsp neutral oil For the sauce: 2 tbsp soy sauce · 1 tsp sesame oil · 1 tsp mirin\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"76\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:74\" name=\"Recipe (02) · directions\" x=\"0\" y=\"678\" width=\"420\" height=\"296\">\n          <text id=\"8:75\" name=\"Recipe (02) · directions\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:76\" name=\"1. Prepare the ingredients — Cut the asparagus, slice the spring onions and beat the eggs. Mix the soy sauce, sesame oil and mirin in a small bowl. [Photo_Cooking_Step] Day-old rice works best: it is drier, so the grains fry separately instead of turning mushy. Break up any clumps before you start. 2. Cook the eggs and asparagus — Heat the oil in a wok over high heat. Scramble the eggs until just set, push them to the side, then stir-fry the asparagus for 2 minutes until bright green and still crisp. 3. Fry the rice and season — Add the rice and toss for 3–4 minutes until hot and lightly toasted. Pour over the sauce, fold in the eggs and spring onions, and serve right away.\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"228\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:77\" name=\"Articles (03, in order)\" x=\"444\" y=\"678\" width=\"420\" height=\"467\">\n          <text id=\"8:78\" name=\"Articles (03, in order)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"148\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:79\" name=\"All dated 12 November 2021. 1. Crochet Projects for Noodle Lovers · Wade Warren (Photo_Chicken_Ramen, Avatar_Wade_Warren) — Our favourite slurpable noodle bowls, from quick ramen to slow-simmered broths. 2. 10 Vegetarian Recipes To Eat This Month · Robert Fox (Photo_Tropical_Fruit_Salad, Avatar_Robert_Fox) — Seasonal, meat-free dishes that are colourful, filling and easy to make. 3. Full Guide to Becoming a Professional Chef · Dianne Russell (Photo_Blog_Chef, Avatar_Dianne_Russell) — A working head chef on first jobs, long services and what it really takes. 4. Simple &amp; Delicious Vegetarian Lasagna · Leslie Alexander (Photo_Vegetarian_Lasagna, Avatar_Leslie_Alexander) — Layers of roasted vegetables, rich tomato sauce and creamy béchamel. 5. Plantain and Pinto Stew with Aji Verde · Courtney Henry (Photo_Plantain_Stew, Avatar_Courtney_Henry) — A hearty one-pot stew finished with a bright, herby green sauce. 6. We’re Hiring a Communications Assistant! · Albert Flores (Photo_Hiring, Avatar_Albert_Flores) — Love food and words? Join our small team and help us tell more food stories.\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"399\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:80\" name=\"Blog post (04) · header &amp; Q1–Q2\" x=\"888\" y=\"678\" width=\"420\" height=\"315\">\n          <text id=\"8:81\" name=\"Blog post (04) · header &amp; Q1–Q2\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"218\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:82\" name=\"Intro: We asked a working head chef about first jobs, long services and what it really takes to make it in a professional kitchen. How did you start out in the food industry? — I started washing dishes in a small family restaurant when I was sixteen. Watching the line cooks every night made me want to be on the other side of the pass, and after two years the chef finally let me prep vegetables. What do you like most about your job? — The rhythm of service. Hours of preparation come down to a few intense minutes, and when a full dining room goes quiet because everyone is eating, it feels like the whole team has done something together.\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"247\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:83\" name=\"Blog post (04) · Q3–Q5 &amp; quote\" x=\"0\" y=\"1169\" width=\"420\" height=\"353\">\n          <text id=\"8:84\" name=\"Blog post (04) · Q3–Q5 &amp; quote\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"212\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:85\" name=\"Do you cook at home on your days off? — Yes, but simply. I cook the food I grew up with: rice, eggs and whatever vegetables look good at the market. Home cooking is where I remember why I love food. [Photo_Cooking_Step] What would your advice be to young people looking to get their foot in the door? — Start anywhere and be the person who shows up early. Ask questions, taste everything and write down what you learn. Pull quote: “Technique can be taught; curiosity and reliability can’t.” What is the biggest misconception that people have about being a professional chef? — That it is all creativity. Most of the job is consistency: making the same dish perfectly two hundred times a night, keeping the kitchen clean and looking after your team.\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"285\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:86\" name=\"Newsletter (all frames)\" x=\"444\" y=\"1169\" width=\"420\" height=\"144\">\n          <text id=\"8:87\" name=\"Newsletter (all frames)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:88\" name=\"Deliciousness to your inbox Get new recipes and cooking tips in your inbox every week. No spam, unsubscribe anytime. Your email address... · Subscribe\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"76\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:89\" name=\"Footer (all frames)\" x=\"888\" y=\"1169\" width=\"420\" height=\"144\">\n          <text id=\"8:90\" name=\"Footer (all frames)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:91\" name=\"Logo_Foodieland · “Simple, tasty recipes for every day.” Links: Recipes · Blog · Contact · About us “© 2020 Foodieland. All rights reserved.” · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"76\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"8:92\" name=\"What is fixed · what is yours\" x=\"64\" y=\"4439\" width=\"1312\" height=\"332\">\n      <text id=\"8:93\" name=\"What is fixed · what is yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"328\" height=\"35\" />\n      <frame id=\"8:94\" name=\"Fixed vs yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"281\">\n        <frame id=\"8:95\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"221\">\n          <text id=\"8:96\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"8:97\" name=\"• Frame list and exact names • Must-include content per frame (what, not how) • Navigation structure and links • All data and copy • Brand colors #000000 and #E7F9FD, and Inter • Media: wordmark, social logos, photos, category images, decorations, avatars, icons • Default Button, default Text Field\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"140\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:98\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"668\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"281\">\n          <text id=\"8:99\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"197\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"8:100\" name=\"• Layout, grid, grouping, order and emphasis on every page • All other colors: neutrals, text, other backgrounds / surfaces, favorite / like color, links, error / disabled • Type scale, spacing, radii, elevation • All states: current nav item, favorited card, checked item, current page, focused field, hover • Header, footer, featured recipe, category tile, recipe card, promo card, Instagram post, newsletter card, recipe meta, nutrition panel, ingredient checklist, direction step, article list item, sidebar lists, search bar, pagination, article layout, pull quote, form, select • How photos and cut-outs are cropped and placed\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"200\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"8:101\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"64\" y=\"4819\" width=\"1312\" height=\"281\">\n      <text id=\"8:102\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"222\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"8:103\" name=\"Your file is compared with this brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any original.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <text id=\"8:104\" name=\"1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data &amp; copy accuracy 3. Flow &amp; prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality &amp; consistency of your own system 6. Component reuse 7. State design (current nav, favorited, checked, current page)\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"154\" />\n      <text id=\"8:105\" name=\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 5 named frames, your components and the prototype.\" x=\"0\" y=\"259\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n    </frame>\n  </frame>\n</canvas>"},{"type":"text","text":"IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design, since this tool only returns metadata. If you do not call get_design_context, the agent will not be able to implement the design."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a1094b8-95cb-47b4-aa0a-0df7e190b320","uuid":"861e52e4-d681-4ebc-b04d-fb620f31e290","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:02:57.516Z","tool_use_result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<canvas id=\"0:1\" name=\"00 · Start Here 设计任务\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\">\n  <frame id=\"8:2\" name=\"Start Here · Brief\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1440\" height=\"5164\">\n    <frame id=\"8:3\" name=\"Header\" x=\"64\" y=\"64\" width=\"1312\" height=\"145\">\n      <text id=\"8:4\" name=\"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"182\" height=\"19\" />\n      <text id=\"8:5\" name=\"Foodieland — recipe and food blog website\" x=\"0\" y=\"31\" width=\"1312\" height=\"52\" />\n      <text id=\"8:6\" name=\"Design a recipe website: discover featured and popular recipes, open a recipe with its ingredients and directions, browse and read blog articles, and contact the team. Desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\" x=\"0\" y=\"95\" width=\"1312\" height=\"50\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"8:7\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"64\" y=\"257\" width=\"1312\" height=\"249\">\n      <text id=\"8:8\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"147\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"8:9\" name=\"1. Build exactly the 5 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The two brand colors and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button and a default Text Field. Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the wordmark, the social logos, the photos, the category images, the decorations, the avatars and the icons from 04 · Media. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"198\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"8:10\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\"64\" y=\"554\" width=\"1312\" height=\"1925\">\n      <text id=\"8:11\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"413\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"8:12\" name=\"Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <frame id=\"8:13\" name=\"Frame cards\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"1836\">\n        <frame id=\"8:14\" name=\"01_Home\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"756\">\n          <text id=\"8:15\" name=\"01_Home\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"82\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"8:16\" name=\"Goal: Find something to cook today.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:17\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:18\" name=\"• Categories: “Categories” · “View All Categories” · Breakfast · Vegan · Meat · Dessert · Lunch · Chocolate, each with its image (Category_Breakfast … Category_Chocolate) • Chef promo: “Everyone can be a chef in their own kitchen” · copy (see DATA) · “Learn More” · Photo_Chef · Decor_Tomato · Decor_Onion • Featured recipe: “Hot Recipes” (Icon_Hot_Recipes) · “Spicy delicious chicken wings” · copy (see DATA) · 30 Minutes (Icon_Timer) · Chicken (Icon_Fork_Knife) · Avatar_John_Smith · John Smith · 15 March 2022 · “View Recipes” (Icon_Play) · Photo_Hero_Chicken_Wings · round badge “Handpicked Recipes” • Footer: see DATA (Footer) • Header: Logo_Foodieland · navigation Home / Recipes / Blog / Contact / About us · current: Home · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram • Instagram: “Check out @foodieland on Instagram” · copy (see DATA) · 4 posts, each with Avatar_Foodieland · “Foodieland.” · “Tokyo, Japan” · more (Icon_More) · photo · photo counter 1/3 · like (Icon_Like) · comment (Icon_Comment) · share (Icon_Send) · save (Icon_Save) · “Liked by craig_love and 44,686 others” · caption · “September 19” (see DATA) · “Visit Our Instagram” (Logo_Instagram) • More recipes: “Try this delicious recipe to make your day” · copy (see DATA) · 8 recipe cards with photo, title, time (Icon_Timer), category (Icon_Fork_Knife) and favorite (Icon_Favorite) · favorited: as marked in DATA • Newsletter: “Deliciousness to your inbox” · copy (see DATA) · email field “Your email address...” · “Subscribe” · Decor_Subscribe_Vegetables · Decor_Subscribe_Leaf · Decor_Subscribe_Salad • Simple and tasty recipes: “Simple and tasty recipes” · copy (see DATA) · 8 recipe cards with photo, title, time (Icon_Timer), category (Icon_Fork_Knife) and favorite (Icon_Favorite) · favorited: as marked in DATA · promo card: “Don’t forget to eat healthy food” · “www.foodieland.com” · Photo_Ad_Salad\" x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"596\" height=\"520\" />\n          <text id=\"8:19\" name=\"LINKS\" x=\"24\" y=\"646\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:20\" name=\"→ “Healthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus” card → 02_Recipe → Blog (nav) → 03_Blog → Contact (nav) → 05_Contact\" x=\"24\" y=\"672\" width=\"596\" height=\"60\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"8:21\" name=\"02_Recipe\" x=\"668\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"716\">\n          <text id=\"8:22\" name=\"02_Recipe\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"93\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"8:23\" name=\"Goal: Follow the recipe for Healthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"8:24\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"8:25\" name=\"• Actions: “PRINT” (Icon_Print) · “SHARE” (Icon_Share) • Directions: “Directions” · 3 steps, each with checkbox, number, title and text; step 1 also has Photo_Cooking_Step (see DATA) • Footer: see DATA (Footer) • Header: Logo_Foodieland · navigation Home / Recipes / Blog / Contact / About us · current: Recipes · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram • Ingredients: “Ingredients” · “For main dish” 5 items · “For the sauce” 3 items · each with a checkbox · checked: the first main-dish item (Icon_Check) (see DATA) • Intro: one paragraph (see DATA) • Media: Photo_Japanese_Fried_Rice as the recipe video cover · play (Icon_Play) • Meta: Avatar_John_Smith · John Smith · 15 March 2022 · “PREP TIME” 15 Minutes (Icon_Timer) · “COOK TIME” 15 Minutes (Icon_Timer) · Healthy (Icon_Fork_Knife) • Newsletter: “Deliciousness to your inbox” · copy (see DATA) · email field “Your email address...” · “Subscribe” · Decor_Subscribe_Vegetables · Decor_Subscribe_Leaf · Decor_Subscribe_Salad • Nutrition Information: Calories 219.9 kcal · Total Fat 10.7 g · Protein 7.9 g · Carbohydrate 22.3 g · Cholesterol 37.4 mg · note (see DATA) • Other Recipe: “Other Recipe” · Chick