{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgQMkoakNdoaBehVtj6lp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about a Figma plugin build error: \"New parent is an instance or is inside of an instance\" at the `const cta=F(hl,...)` call. I trace which parents the `F` helper appends into: `hero` goes into `home`, a frame, so that parent is valid. The failing child sits inside `hl`, so `hl` itself must have landed inside an instance. The only instance on the page is `hdrInst`, the Header instance created with `inst(home,'13:20')`, where 13:20 is Site / Header. If `hero` or `hl` is appended to `hdrInst` rather than to `home`, the error matches. I check the other outputs too: the Button set measures 126x62, the Category tile set shows one tile, the Recipe card set is 302 wide (correct), Footer height 300 with the tagline clipped, and Newsletter looks broken with the title cut off. I rebuild 01_Home from scratch, order the appends so every section frame joins `home` and never the Header instance, set layoutMode VERTICAL with primaryAxisSizingMode 'AUTO' so height hugs, and use 4 columns of 302 with 24 gaps for 1280 content. Then I build Home part A (hero, categories, chef promo) and part B (recipe grids, instagram, newsletter, footer).","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":15561,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":114994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15561}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a1094b8-95cb-47b4-aa0a-0df7e190b320","uuid":"3c4d3ea2-4dc2-463e-a8be-fd604195fbfd","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:16:56.029Z","thinking_duration_ms":36498}
