{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgQOKv7ypfM1mjF1jSPh3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to fix five visual defects in a Figma build: the recipe page title/meta collision, the direction step body overlap, the blog article card text overlap, the blog search bar overlapping the first article, and the blog post Q&A paragraph overlap.\n\nLet me work the first fix. The recipe title at 50px with width 980 wraps to 2 lines, ending around y=263, which collides with meta at y=238. I drop the title to 44px, set width 1100 and x=170, so it fits on 1 line ending near y=206. Meta at 238, intro at 318 and media at 424 then clear each other.\n\nFor fix 2, the direction step's Body frame is fixed at 140 height, so text overflows. I set the step component's counterAxisSizingMode to AUTO and give Body vertical auto layout with primaryAxisSizingMode AUTO, keeping width 700 for the texts.\n\nFor fix 3, the article card uses absolute positions with text heights measured after setting characters. Card is 416x470: photo 416x240 at (0,0), title at (26,258) width 364 at 21px, excerpt at (26,330) width 364 at 14px, author row at (26,390) height 32 with avatar 32 and name/date stacked beside it at x=48.\n\nFor fix 4, the search bar was scaled by 880/420, giving height 125.7 and bottom 445.7, which overlaps articles at 412. Instead I resize the instance frame to 880x64 so the inner placeholder grows via layoutGrow, then start articles at 410.\n\nFor fix 5, the Q&A paragraphs overlap because auto-layout heights go stale. I rebuild ArticleBody as a plain frame with manual stacking: each text is created, characters and font set, width resized, then its measured height read and the cursor advanced by height plus gap 26. This is deterministic and needs no auto-layout recompute.\n\nThe blog grid row pitch becomes 470+48=518, so pagination sits at 410+3*518+20=1984 and the newsletter at 2070.","si